  "summary": {
    "en": "Libyan forces have compelled Haftar militia members to surrender at a strategic airbase while continuing artillery attacks on Haftar posts. Turkish officials have publicly welcomed a motion supporting Libyan troops, indicating external political backing. China is re-engaging in Libya with military forces tied to recent business agreements, adding a new foreign military dimension. The United Nations has introduced laws criminalising child conscription and raising the recruitment age to 18. There were 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.",
